WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
- Are you like this-
because I hate acting,

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.090
but I love-

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:05.340
I feel like I do it on stage
cause you jump into character

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.401
of wherever you were
when you wrote the song.

00:00:06.401 --> 00:00:07.234
- [Ann] Right. Yeah, yeah.

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:08.850
- Is that ever hard for you?

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.020
Depending upon this song?

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:10.853
Like, you know, like-

00:00:10.853 --> 00:00:13.230
- For me it's not the
songs that are too intense,

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.390
It's the ones that I've grown out of.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.223
- [Kelly] Ah.

00:00:16.223 --> 00:00:17.056
- Like, you know,

00:00:17.056 --> 00:00:19.920
I don't wanna say anything
about too specific songs, but-

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.630
- You don't want to like poo
poo on the songs, but yeah.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.160
- But a song like "Magic Man", you know?

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:23.993
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:23.993 --> 00:00:27.300
- Was written way back when I
was in my super early twenties

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.770
and with my first love and-

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:30.341
- Don't you bash "Magic
Man" right now, ma'am.

00:00:30.341 --> 00:00:31.424
- (laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:00:31.424 --> 00:00:32.257
- I will-
- That's what I meant,

00:00:32.257 --> 00:00:34.020
yeah.
- I will actually tackle you.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.785
- That's what I meant. I don't
wanna bash any song, but-

00:00:35.785 --> 00:00:36.618
- You know why?

00:00:36.618 --> 00:00:38.580
I think it was actually the
first Heart song I ever heard,

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.413
as a child.

00:00:39.413 --> 00:00:40.350
And I was like-

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.350
and it, honestly it was
because it was women.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.183
- Yeah.

00:00:44.183 --> 00:00:46.110
- And usually you always heard
men doing the rock stuff.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.510
And so, I remember- cause my
brother's like a decade older,

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.580
anything they were listening
to was always like men-

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.230
And I was like, wait, what? I can do this?

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.090
And it was like representation
at its finest point.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:54.923
I was like, wait.
- [Ann] Right.

00:00:54.923 --> 00:00:57.150
- Women are able to do this
too? And it was really cool.

00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:00.060
Cause I feel like y'all
opened the door for all the-

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:00.960
for the Alanis Morissettes-

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.520
for all these women in music later on.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:03.360
(audience applauds)

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.120
So next year is the 50th
anniversary of Heart.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:06.953
- [Ann] Yeah.

00:01:06.953 --> 00:01:08.236
- So that's amazing.

00:01:08.236 --> 00:01:09.569
(audience applauds)

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.610
So, do you have any plans to celebrate?

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.260
I mean that's awesome. 50 years?

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.093
- We do.

00:01:14.093 --> 00:01:14.926
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- But,

00:01:14.926 --> 00:01:18.600
I gotta say it's too early days
for me to talk about it now.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:19.433
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:20.580
- I'm not at liberty to discuss it.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.555
- Oh, I like it.

00:01:21.555 --> 00:01:22.431
- But- (laughs)

00:01:22.431 --> 00:01:23.264
(audience laughs)
- Yeah, that makes it a tease.

00:01:23.264 --> 00:01:24.630
- But yeah, yeah.
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:26.010
- Yeah. We are gonna do a thing.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:27.863
- [Kelly] Okay, just asking for a friend.

